# Importer architecture diagram

`docs/import-architecture.md` is the single picture of how the job URL importer
works. It must never drift from the code.

When you change the importer (new source, adapter, fallback step, guard, limit,
queue, route or UI hand-off), update the doc **in the same commit**:

1. **Diagram**: add, remove or re-wire nodes in the mermaid flowchart so the
   arrows match the code's real order. Solid edges are built; dotted edges are
   planned only.
2. **Tables**: "Sources of company and title", "Limits and guards", "Not built".
3. **Changelog**: one line per change, newest last.
4. Check the diagram renders: keep node labels in quotes, no stray `(` or `;`
   outside quotes.

Before finishing a task that touched these files, re-read the diagram against
the code. If a box or arrow no longer matches, fix the doc, not just the code.

Also keep the "Not built" list honest: remove an item when it ships.
